        "Alexei Kitaev",
        "Andrew M. Steane",
        "Peter W. Shor"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction showed how quantum information can be protected despite noise and supplied essential concepts for fault-tolerant quantum physics.",
        "attribution": "Shor and Steane introduced influential error-correcting codes, while Kitaev developed topological approaches that reshaped fault-tolerant computation.",
        "maturity": "Logical qubits and error-suppression milestones have been demonstrated, but large-scale fault-tolerant computation has not yet been achieved.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The scientific recognition due to theoretical foundations versus ongoing experimental establishment of scalable correction is not yet settled."
        ]
      }
    },
