        "Hidetoshi Katori",
        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks enabled unprecedented precision in time measurement and opened sensitive tests of fundamental physics and relativistic effects.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye made complementary foundational contributions to the lattice-clock concept and its experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "The technology is highly mature, with independent implementations and sustained improvements in accuracy and stability.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broad development of optical frequency standards involved many contributors beyond the two proposed names."
        ]
      }
    },
