        "Fedor Jelezko",
        "Jörg Wrachtrup",
        "Mikhail D. Lukin"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical control and readout of diamond spins made single solid-state defects into practical quantum sensors and a versatile setting for studying spin coherence.",
        "attribution": "Jelezko and Wrachtrup established key optical experiments with diamond defects, while Lukin contributed influential quantum-control and sensing concepts.",
        "maturity": "The physics is well established and reproduced, with sensing demonstrations across laboratories; the range of applications continues to develop.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The achievement encompasses several distinct milestones in defect discovery, control, and sensing, complicating a single prize boundary."
        ]
      }
    },
