        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation and the quantum origin of primordial structure provide a deep framework linking early-universe physics to the observed large-scale cosmos.",
        "attribution": "Guth and Linde developed central inflationary ideas, while Mukhanov made foundational contributions to the theory of primordial perturbations.",
        "maturity": "The framework has strong indirect support from cosmological observations, but decisive evidence for inflation itself and its specific mechanism remains absent.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Many inflationary models can fit current observations, and the quantum origin of structure has not been isolated as a unique empirical signature."
        ]
      }
